Subject: [PATCH] fix: tolerate strict-schema empty arrays and expose todo
 patch properties
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: allow strict-schema models to use todo full and patch modes without false mode conflicts or missing update fields
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-fix
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1012-personal-fix-support-strict-schema-todo-payloads.patch

Patch intent:
Ignore empty sibling arrays (`[]`) when determining whether a `todo` call uses
full-list replacement or `update`/`add`/`remove` patch mode, and declare explicit
item properties on `update` and `add` in the `todo` parameter schema.

Why it exists:
Providers that enforce strict JSON schemas require models to emit every top-level
property on tool calls (sending `[]` for unused array parameters) and strip or
ignore `additionalProperties: true` on `update` and `add` items. Previously,
`apply_todo_patch` treated any non-null `update`/`add`/`remove` array—including
`[]`—as active patch mode and rejected calls that also supplied `todos`, while
`update` items only declared `id` in `properties`, preventing strict-schema
models from updating `status` or `completion_confidence`.

Upstream integration points:
Relies on `todo_write_mode`, `apply_todo_patch`, and `TodoTool::parameters_schema`
in `crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/todo.rs`.

Update guidance:
Preserve the conflict error when both a non-empty `todos` array and a non-empty
patch array (`update`, `add`, or `remove`) are supplied. Keep `update` and `add`
item property schemas aligned with `todos` item properties.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core tool::todo::tests --lib
